    "id": "git-undo-last-commit",
    "title": "How to Undo the Last Commit in Git (Keep or Discard Changes)",
    "excerpt": "Undo a Git commit safely. Use reset to keep or drop changes, revert for pushed commits, amend for small fixes, and reflog to recover.",
    "category": "Coding",
    "date": "November 11, 2026",
