        "question": "Why does Bitcoin use so much more energy than Ethereum?",
        "answer": "Bitcoin uses proof of work, where miners spend electricity to secure the network. Ethereum moved to proof of stake in 2022, which secures the network with locked-up coins instead of computing power."
